1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,064
This is FinPilot HomeLoan, by team
DoubleStack.

2
00:00:03,064 --> 00:00:05,818
It turns a home-loan file into an
explainable,

3
00:00:05,818 --> 00:00:10,548
RBI aligned credit decision in seconds, while
the underwriter stays in control.

4
00:00:11,148 --> 00:00:15,794
The pipeline shows every case: outcome, risk
grade, fraud flags and turnaround.

5
00:00:15,794 --> 00:00:20,968
12 synthetic Indian personas are preloaded,
from salaried and self-employed borrowers to

6
00:00:20,968 --> 00:00:23,791
loans against property and a forged salary
slip.

7
00:00:26,472 --> 00:00:28,309
Let's underwrite a new case.

8
00:00:28,309 --> 00:00:33,952
The relationship manager picks the applicant,
loads PAN, masked Aadhaar, salary slips,

9
00:00:33,952 --> 00:00:39,464
Form 16, 6 months of bank statements and the
property papers, and runs underwriting.

10
00:00:40,064 --> 00:00:45,036
A LangGraph underwriting copilot orchestrates
11 steps: document AI with OCR,

11
00:00:45,036 --> 00:00:50,782
cross-checks and tampering heuristics, bank
analytics, eligibility, fraud and compliance,

12
00:00:50,782 --> 00:00:55,366
a calibrated risk model, a Monte Carlo
capacity test, and the decision.

13
00:00:55,967 --> 00:00:58,819
Karthik's FOIR would be 79% against a 60%
cap,

14
00:00:58,819 --> 00:01:01,423
because of a car loan and a personal loan.

15
00:01:01,423 --> 00:01:06,135
So the engine approves with conditions:
reduce the amount to about ₹37 lakh,

16
00:01:06,135 --> 00:01:09,049
or add a co-applicant, or close existing
loans.

17
00:01:09,049 --> 00:01:11,095
Every reason is in plain English.

18
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:16,621
The underwriter sees each document beside its
extracted fields, OCR confidence and

19
00:01:16,621 --> 00:01:21,066
cross-document checks on name, date of birth,
employer and salary credits.

20
00:01:21,066 --> 00:01:23,469
PAN and Aadhaar are masked at ingestion.

21
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:30,130
The LightGBM model gives a calibrated
probability of default with SHAP reasons,

22
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:35,015
and FinPilot's Monte Carlo stress test checks
repayment capacity after the new EMI.

23
00:01:35,015 --> 00:01:37,311
Policy rules always dominate the model.

24
00:01:37,912 --> 00:01:43,819
Every rule fired carries its policy rule ID
and regulatory citation, such as the RBI

25
00:01:43,819 --> 00:01:48,953
Housing Finance Company Directions 2025, para
58, for loan-to-value caps.

26
00:01:49,554 --> 00:01:51,956
The underwriter can question the copilot.

27
00:01:51,956 --> 00:01:57,053
Answers are grounded only in the case data
and the policy file, and they cite rule IDs.

28
00:01:57,053 --> 00:01:59,806
It works offline, or with a local Ollama
model.

29
00:02:04,495 --> 00:02:08,084
The underwriter can override any decision,
but must record a reason.

30
00:02:08,084 --> 00:02:10,934
The override is written to a hash-chained
audit trail,

31
00:02:10,934 --> 00:02:14,259
and the credit memo and sanction letter draft
update instantly.

32
00:02:21,185 --> 00:02:22,754
Here is the fraud persona.

33
00:02:22,754 --> 00:02:27,219
The salary slip was edited in iLovePDF, the
net pay uses a different font,

34
00:02:27,219 --> 00:02:29,994
and bank credits are half the declared
income.

35
00:02:29,994 --> 00:02:32,528
The engine declines, with written reasons.

36
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:35,418
FinPilot HomeLoan: faster turnaround,

37
00:02:35,418 --> 00:02:39,437
consistent policy and audit-ready files for
Hero Housing Finance.

38
00:02:39,437 --> 00:02:44,261
Decision support for underwriters; final
decisions follow the lender's policy.

39
00:02:44,261 --> 00:02:44,879
Thank you.
